{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block content %}

<section class="mb-8">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">What can these providers actually prove?</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700 max-w-3xl">
    Every day we ask each confidential-inference provider for an attestation and check what it
    contains. A row is <strong>verified</strong> only when every layer that provider's architecture
    <em>should</em> be able to prove, it proves. Anything we could not reach is marked as such
    rather than scored — an unreachable endpoint is not a privacy finding.
    <a class="underline" href="./methodology.html">Methodology →</a>
  </p>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
{# Calibration. A detector that has never fired is the first thing a   #}
{# reader should know about, not something to bury.                    #}
{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
<section class="mb-8 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5">
  <h2 class="text-sm uppercase font-semibold tracking-wider text-slate-500">How much to trust this page</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-800">
    Over <strong>{{ quality.window.days }} days</strong> and
    <strong>{{ quality.calibration.observations }} observations</strong>, this instrument has
    produced <strong>{{ quality.calibration['verification-failure'] }} verification failures</strong>.
    Every failing observation in its history was a transport error
    ({{ quality.calibration.transport }}) or an invalid response with no recorded reason
    ({{ quality.calibration['no-error-invalid'] }}).
    {% if quality.calibration['verification-failure'] == 0 %}
    By the rule of three, zero events in {{ quality.calibration.observations }} trials puts the
    95% upper bound on the per-observation verification-failure rate at
    <strong>{{ quality.calibration.rate_upper_bound_95 }}%</strong>. That is the honest reading:
    not "providers are safe", but "if this check fails, it fails less often than about once in
    {{ (quality.calibration.observations // 3) }} observations — or it is not wired to anything."
    We cannot yet distinguish those two cases.
    {% endif %}
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-8 grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Targets verified</div>
    <div class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-1">{{ quality.coverage_summary.get('verified', 0) }} / {{ quality.coverage|length }}</div>
    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">{{ quality.coverage_summary.get('partial', 0) }} partial ·
      {{ quality.coverage_summary.get('unreachable', 0) + quality.coverage_summary.get('invalid', 0) }} unreachable</div>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Builds reviewed</div>
    <div class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-1 {% if quality.audit_debt.backlog > 5 %}text-rose-700{% endif %}">
      {{ quality.audit_debt.builds_reviewed }} / {{ quality.audit_debt.builds_observed }}</div>
    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">backlog {{ quality.audit_debt.backlog }} ·
      last {{ quality.audit_debt.days_since_last_audit }}d ago</div>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Cells carrying signal</div>
    <div class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-1">{{ (quality.density.signal_fraction * 100)|round|int }}%</div>
    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">{{ quality.density.dashes }} of
      {{ quality.density.published_cells }} matrix cells are dashes</div>
  </div>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Unmeasurable providers</div>
    <div class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-1">{{ quality.unmeasurable_providers|length }}</div>
    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">{{ quality.unmeasurable_providers|join(", ") }} expose no
      stable version identity</div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
{# Primary readout: one line per target, a fraction, and what's missing #}
{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Coverage by target</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">
    <strong>Proven</strong> counts the layers this provider's shape is expected to prove — the
    expectation is set per architecture in
    <code>REQUIRED_LAYERS_BY_SHAPE</code>, and that bar is an editorial judgment, not a
    measurement. Different providers have different denominators, so compare the
    <em>missing</em> column, not the fraction alone.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <table class="min-w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Provider</th>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Model</th>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Status</th>
          <th class="text-center p-2">Proven</th>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Unproven / reason</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for r in rows %}
        <tr class="border-t border-slate-100">
          <td class="p-2 font-medium">{{ r.provider }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 font-mono text-xs">{{ r.model }}</td>
          <td class="p-2">
            <span class="inline-block rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs {{ r.status_class }}"
                  title="{{ r.status_title }}">{{ r.status_label }}</span>
          </td>
          <td class="p-2 text-center font-mono text-xs">
            {% if r.status in ("unreachable", "invalid") %}—
            {% else %}{{ r.proven }}/{{ r.required }}
              {% if r.bar.disputed %}<span class="text-rose-700" title="{{ r.bar.note }}">⚠</span>{% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          </td>
          <td class="p-2 text-xs text-slate-600">
            {% if r.status in ("unreachable", "invalid") %}
              <span class="font-mono">{{ (r.error or "no response")[:90] }}</span>
            {% elif r.missing %}
              <span class="font-mono">{{ r.missing|join(", ") }}</span>
            {% else %}—{% endif %}
            {% if r.hidden_layers %}
              <div class="mt-1 text-amber-700">not shown on the matrix below:
                <span class="font-mono">{{ r.hidden_layers|join(", ") }}</span></div>
            {% endif %}
            {% if r.bar.disputed and r.status not in ("unreachable", "invalid") %}
              <div class="mt-1 text-rose-700">{{ r.bar.note }}</div>
            {% endif %}
          </td>
        </tr>
      {% else %}
        <tr><td colspan="5" class="p-4 text-center text-slate-400">no snapshot data</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
{# The dataset that was collected for 111 days and never published.    #}
{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">How often does the attested code change?</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">
    Any client that pins an enclave measurement is betting the measurement holds still. It does not.
    <strong>Deploys</strong> counts transitions to a version string never seen before.
    <strong>Corrected</strong> accounts for deploys that begin and end between two probes:
    with T deploys seen over n−1 daily intervals the rate estimate is −ln(1−T/(n−1))/Δ.
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">
    Read <strong>revisits</strong> only on <code>instance-sampled</code> rows. There the version
    comes from whichever backend answered, so a return to an earlier value means we reached a
    different instance — Chutes' 19 revisits are one deploy plus a fleet that never finished
    draining, not 19 rollouts. On <code>control-plane</code> rows the version is read from a
    single document (NEAR from the gateway's compose, Tinfoil from the release feed), so it
    cannot show fleet structure at all and zero revisits there is guaranteed by construction
    rather than observed. Fleet size is not identifiable from once-a-day sampling on any row.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <table class="min-w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Target</th>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Version source</th>
          <th class="text-right p-2">Observations</th>
          <th class="text-right p-2">Distinct versions</th>
          <th class="text-right p-2">Deploys</th>
          <th class="text-right p-2">Revisits</th>
          <th class="text-right p-2">Days per deploy</th>
          <th class="text-right p-2">Corrected</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for c in quality.cadence %}
        <tr class="border-t border-slate-100">
          <td class="p-2 font-mono text-xs">{{ c.provider }}/{{ c.model }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-xs {% if c.version_source == 'control-plane' %}text-slate-400{% endif %}">{{ c.version_source }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right">{{ c.observations }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right">{{ c.distinct }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right font-semibold">{{ c.novel }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right {% if c.version_source != 'instance-sampled' %}text-slate-300{% elif c.revisit > c.novel %}text-amber-700{% endif %}"
              {% if c.version_source != 'instance-sampled' %}title="control-plane version string — revisits are not meaningful here"{% endif %}>{{ c.revisit }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right">{{ c.days_per_deploy or "—" }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-right font-semibold">{{ c.days_per_deploy_corrected or "—" }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
{# The per-layer matrix, demoted to detail.                            #}
{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Per-layer detail</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">
    Cells:
    <span class="inline-block rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-700">✅</span> verified,
    <span class="inline-block rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs bg-rose-500/20 text-rose-700">❌</span> rejected,
    <span class="inline-block rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 ring-1 ring-amber-300">○</span> awaiting our review,
    <span class="inline-block rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs bg-rose-500/10 text-rose-700 ring-1 ring-rose-200">—</span> required but not exposed,
    <span class="inline-block rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-slate-400">—</span> not applicable to this architecture.
    This matrix shows {{ SCORECARD_LABELS|length }} of the 15 layers the probe records; the
    remainder are listed per row in the coverage table above.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <table class="min-w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Provider</th>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Model</th>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Shape</th>
          {% for key, label in SCORECARD_LABELS.items() %}
          <th class="p-2 text-center" title="{{ SCORECARD_TOOLTIPS[key] }}">{{ label }}</th>
          {% endfor %}
          <th class="p-2 text-right">lat</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for r in rows %}
        <tr class="border-t border-slate-100 {% if r.status in ('unreachable', 'invalid') %}bg-slate-50 text-slate-400{% endif %}">
          <td class="p-2 font-medium">{{ r.provider }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 font-mono text-xs">{{ r.model }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-xs text-slate-500">{{ r.attestation_type or "—" }}</td>
          {% for key in SCORECARD_LABELS %}
          <td class="p-2 text-center">
            <span class="inline-block rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs {{ r.cells[key].class }}" title="{{ r.cells[key].title }}">{{ r.cells[key].mark }}</span>
          </td>
          {% endfor %}
          <td class="p-2 text-right text-xs text-slate-500">{{ r.latency_s }}s</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
{# Editorial. Hand-written, therefore dated and labelled as such.      #}
{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Editorial notes</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-3">
    Hand-written, not computed, and therefore able to go stale. Each carries the date it was last
    checked against the data. Anything not on this list that you see above is machine-derived.
  </p>
  <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-800">
    {% for note in EDITORIAL_NOTES %}
    <li class="flex gap-2">
      <span class="text-slate-400 font-mono text-xs whitespace-nowrap pt-0.5">{{ note.checked }}</span>
      <span><strong>{{ note.title }}</strong> {{ note.body }}</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="text-sm text-slate-600">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-slate-900">How this page is generated</h2>
  <p>
    Daily at 13:17 UTC,
    <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/amiller/awesome-private-inference/actions/workflows/probe-daily.yml"><code>probe-daily.yml</code></a>
    runs <code>python -m probes.collect</code>, writes <code>data/snapshots/YYYY-MM-DD.json</code>,
    recomputes <code>data/quality.json</code> (the self-check driving the four tiles above),
    re-renders this page, and commits. Reproduce with
    <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/amiller/awesome-private-inference#run-a-probe-locally">run a probe locally</a>;
    grade this page with <code>python -m probes.quality</code>.
  </p>
</section>

{% endblock %}
